      <!-- Section 5: What Not to Do Before Selling Your Sebring Home: Costly Mistakes to Avoid -->
      <section class="mb-14 space-y-5 text-stone-700 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-sans" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
        <h2 id="mistakes-heading" class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#1b3a5c]">
          What Not to Do Before Selling Your Sebring Home: Costly Mistakes to Avoid
        </h2>
        <p>
          Steering clear of common pre-listing pitfalls is just as crucial as executing the right marketing plan. In Highlands County, these four mistakes frequently jeopardize seller equity:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
          <div class="p-5 bg-stone-50 rounded-xl border border-stone-200">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-[#1b3a5c] mb-1.5">
              1. Don't Over-Improve with Luxury Remodels
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
              Gutting kitchens or installing luxury tile rarely recoups 100% of costs in Central Florida. Buyers prefer selecting their own finishes. Instead, invest in cost-effective cosmetic updates: warm neutral paint, modern cabinet pulls, fresh mulch, and power-washed driveways.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 bg-stone-50 rounded-xl border border-stone-200">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-[#1b3a5c] mb-1.5">
              2. Never Conceal Roof Age or Prior Water Leaks
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
              Under Florida law (<em>Johnson v. Davis</em>), sellers must disclose known material defects. Buyer insurers require a 4-Point Inspection and Roof Certification. Masking an aging roof leads to collapsed escrows. Disclosing upfront allows us to price strategically or offer closing credits.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 bg-stone-50 rounded-xl border border-stone-200">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-[#1b3a5c] mb-1.5">
              3. Avoid "Testing the Market" with an Inflated Price
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
              The first two weeks on MLS generate your highest buyer enthusiasm. Overpricing by 7% to 10% causes serious buyers to bypass the listing. Extended days on market signal distress, leading to low-ball offers. Accurate upfront pricing ignites urgency and multiple bids.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 bg-stone-50 rounded-xl border border-stone-200">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-[#1b3a5c] mb-1.5">
              4. Don't Attend or Hover During Showings
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
              When sellers remain during walkthroughs, buyers feel hurried and unable to speak candidly or visualize living there. Secure your pets, step out during showings, and allow the buyer and their agent the space to connect with your home.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

